            <h2>Seeing the Landscape Change by Rail </h2>
            <p>The appeal of train travel is that of perspective. The way to Las Vegas frequently goes through spacious plains, desert landscapes, and open landscapes. The changing of the scenery provides the background to the desert-like setting of the city and forms a visual story that cannot be viewed by an air traveler. </p>

